L3.C1 MITgcm-WRF coupled simulation test: Red Sea
==================================================

This directory contains the L3.C1 Red Sea coupling test. ESMF drives MITgcm
and WRF through their initialize, run, and finalize phases. This is a verbose
debug and integration case; it is not a production configuration.

Supported build path
--------------------

The maintained U-004 path is Linux with the ESMF compiler family also used for
MITgcm. The installer recognizes gfortran, intel/ifort, and pgi option files.
The verified reference environment uses gfortran, Open MPI, ESMF 8.9.0, WRF
4.7.1 with the SKRIPS coupling overlay, and MITgcm checkpoint68r.

Use a disposable external copy of this case for each clean build. The installer
creates build/ and code/ and intentionally refuses to reuse either directory;
this prevents stale artifacts from being reported as a successful build.

Required environment
--------------------

Set these variables before installation:

  ESMF_DIR                 ESMF installation root
  ESMF_LIB                 ESMF library directory
  ESMF_MOD                 ESMF module directory
  ESMFMKFILE               absolute path to esmf.mk
  ESMF_OS                  Linux
  ESMF_COMPILER            gfortran, intel/ifort, or pgi
  WRF_DIR                  coupled WRF build directory
  MITGCM_DIR               writable MITgcm source copy
  SKRIPS_MPI_INC           MPI Fortran include/module directory
  SKRIPS_MPI_LIB           MPI library directory
  SKRIPS_NETCDF_INCLUDE    compiler include flags, for example -I/usr/include
  SKRIPS_NETCDF_LIB        linker search flags, for example -L/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu

The installer validates the variables, required files, and build commands
before creating any build directory. Run ./install.sh --help for its interface.

Install
-------

Interactive:

  ./install.sh

Non-interactive/reproducible:

  ./install.sh --yes

Optional build parallelism:

  export MITGCM_BUILD_JOBS=8
  export COUPLER_BUILD_JOBS=1

Any failed prerequisite, compile, archive, or link step returns a non-zero exit
status. A successful install produces:

  build/mitgcmuv
  build/mmout/mitgcm_org_ocn.mod
  build/mmout/libmitgcm_org_ocn.a
  build/mmout/libmitgcmrtl.a
  coupledCode/esmf_application

Run the shortest coupled case
-----------------------------

First generate the WRF initial and boundary files, then run the coupled model:

  cd runCase.init
  ./Allrun
  cd ../runCase
  ./Allrun

Both scripts stop on missing inputs or command failures. They use four MPI ranks
by default. Override the launcher or rank count when needed:

  export MPIEXEC=mpirun
  export SKRIPS_MPI_RANKS=4

Both runners require WRF_DIR and ESMF_LIB. They validate the ESMF library
directory and prepend it to LD_LIBRARY_PATH before launching WRF or the coupled
application, so a fresh shell does not need a separately exported loader path.

runCase/Allrun writes the coupled standard output and error stream to log.esmf
and propagates the MPI exit code. The verified one-hour case reaches MITgcm
checkpoint 60 and WRF model time 2012-06-01_01:00:00 before finalization.

Debugging helpers
-----------------

runMITtest tests MITgcm flux handling. runWRFtest tests WRF flux handling.
latexSummary generates the debug report. The case emits extensive diagnostics
at every coupling interval, so storage use is much higher than a production
run.
